@cc [owner:ykmsd,label:product;react] sparkle-owned-text-translated
Every user-visible string that sparkle supplies itself (JSX text, default labels, placeholders,
tooltips, `aria-label`, `alt`) in a non-story file MUST go through a Lingui macro with the English
text as the message, and a sentence MUST be a single message. A prop default MUST be resolved in the
component body (`label ?? t\`Load more\``), and the prop documented with `@default`. Text passed in
by the consumer through props is the consumer's to translate. Brand names, keyboard symbols and
user content MUST NOT be wrapped. Catalog freshness and completeness are enforced by
`npm run i18n:check`.

@cc [owner:ykmsd,label:coding] sparkle-lingui-macros-only
Sparkle sources MUST only use Lingui through its macros: `useLingui` and the JSX macros (`<Trans>`,
`<Plural>`, `<Select>`, `<SelectOrdinal>`) from `@lingui/react/macro`, and `msg`/`plural`/`select`
from `@lingui/core/macro`. They MUST NOT use the global `t` from `@lingui/core/macro`, or import
`@lingui/react` or `@lingui/core` outside `lib/i18n/`. Enforced by the `noRestrictedImports` Biome
rule on `sparkle/src`.

@cc [owner:ykmsd,label:architecture] macros-compiled-before-jsx
`npm run build:esm` MUST compile Lingui macros, JSX macros included, before compiling JSX.
`scripts/check-esm-macros.mjs` fails the build when a module using a JSX macro had its JSX compiled
first.

@cc [owner:ykmsd,label:architecture] single-lingui-react-copy
`@lingui/react` in sparkle's `dependencies` MUST be the exact version front depends on, so that the
monorepo installs a single copy and sparkle's `useLingui` reads the `LinguiContext` of front's
`I18nProvider`. With two copies sparkle silently renders in English. Covered by
`front/lib/i18n/i18n.test.ts`.
